    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0715" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Ruddock</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-11T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>192. Your telegram 249, July 8, 6 p.m.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d556-f1"/></p>
                <p>Impress upon Chinese Government inadvisability of authorizing any financial
                    commitments which would alter status of rights and interests in Chinese Eastern
                    Railway.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="12" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 238, July 9, from the Chargé in Japan, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
